{number: 35}
{title: Low In The Grave He Lay}
{key: Bb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Bb] Low in the grave He lay, [Eb] Jesus my [Bb] Savior!
[Bb] Waiting the coming day, [Gm] Jesus my [F7] Lord!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Up from the [Bb] grave He a-[F] rose,
With a [Eb] mighty triumph [F7] o'er His [Bb] foes;
He a-[F] rose a Victor from the [Bb] dark domain,
And He [Eb] lives for-[Cm] ever with His [F] saints to reign:
He a-[Bb] rose! He a-[Eb] rose!
Halle-[Bb] lujah! [F7] Christ a-[Bb] rose!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Bb] Vainly they watch His bed, [Eb] Jesus my [Bb] Savior!
[Bb] Vainly they seal the dead, [Gm] Jesus my [F7] Lord!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Bb] Death cannot keep his prey, [Eb] Jesus my [Bb] Savior!
[Bb] He tore the bars away, [Gm] Jesus my [F7] Lord!
{end_of_verse}
